 [patch.crates-io]
+# 32-bit time64: on Debian trixie libasound writes a 16-byte struct timespec,
+# while libc::timespec stays 8 bytes on arm-unknown-linux-gnueabihf, so
+# Status::get_htstamp overruns the frame of whoever called it. alsa-sys 0.6.1
+# grew its own 16-byte timespec and alsa 0.12.1 uses it in place of libc's;
